<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="60308" href="schedule/2014/fall/ESE/497/60308.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2014" href="schedule/2014.xml">2014</calendarYear><term id="120148" href="schedule/2014/fall.xml">Fall 2014</term><subject id="ESE" href="schedule/2014/fall/ESE.xml">Earth, Society, and Environment</subject><course id="497" href="schedule/2014/fall/ESE/497.xml">Special Topics in ESE</course></parents><sectionNumber>A  </sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Dixon Springs Field Trip</sectionTitle><creditHours>1 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>A weekend field trip to Dixon Springs in southern Illinois for ESE majors and professors that investigates the environment of Southern Illinois, examining the ecology, geology and sustainability of the region. Activities will include a writing workshop, a tour of Midwestern forests and wetlands, nature photography, and a geological hike. The trip occurs in late September. Grading will be S/U. The School is subsidizing the  travel costs. There is a field trip fee of $100.</sectionText><sectionFeeAmount>LAS Field Trip $100.00 Flat Fee.</sectionFeeAmount><partOfTerm>A</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>CrossListOpen</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2014-08-25Z</startDate><endDate>2014-10-17Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="CNF">Conference</type><start>05:00 PM</start><end>06:20 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>R      </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>165</roomNumber><buildingName>Noyes Laboratory</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Kanter" firstName="R">Kanter, R</instructor><instructor lastName="Marshak" firstName="S">Marshak, S</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>